course: dictionary
lesson: 8523
title: Sauerkraut and sour cabbage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a word is from another language, and the sentences around it tell you what it means. «Cook fought scurvy with fresh food and sauerkraut.» Scurvy is an illness, and fresh food and sauerkraut are things that fight it, so sauerkraut must be a food.
explain: The dictionary says sauerkraut is cabbage that has been salted and left to ferment until it turns sour. Ferment is the key idea: the cabbage changes slowly, and it tastes sour afterwards.
explain: Lists are context too. «Bacteria also help make cheese, pickles, sauerkraut and sourdough bread.» All of these foods are changed by bacteria, so sauerkraut is one of the foods that bacteria help to make.
fact: Sauerkraut means finely shredded cabbage that has been salted and left to ferment until it is sour.
fact: Sauerkraut is a traditional food in Germany and central and eastern Europe, often eaten with sausages.
fact: Sauerkraut is a German word meaning «sour cabbage».
fact: In fermentation, tiny bacteria turn the sugar in cabbage into acid, which helps keep the food from going bad.
fact: Sailors such as Captain Cook's crew ate sauerkraut to help stop scurvy.
exercise: «Cook fought scurvy with fresh food and sauerkraut.» What is sauerkraut? | A kind of fresh fruit | A German sausage | A sailing ship | *Cabbage that has been salted and left to turn sour
exercise: Sauerkraut is a German word. What does it mean in English? | Hot sausage | Sweet apple | Salted fish | *Sour cabbage
exercise: In sauerkraut, what turns the sugar in the cabbage into acid? | Salt | *Tiny bacteria | Scurvy | Sailors
test: What is the main ingredient of sauerkraut? | Potatoes | Carrots | *Cabbage | Onions
test: Based on Cook's voyage, why did sailors eat sauerkraut? | To make them sleep better | Because it was sweet | *To help fight scurvy | To keep their boats clean
exam: Which sentence best explains what sauerkraut is? | Sauerkraut is a sailing ship | Sauerkraut is a fresh fruit salad | *Sauerkraut is salted, sour cabbage that has been fermented | Sauerkraut is a kind of sausage
